Actually maybe the bug is in suggestEmojis with the trie: for 'eye', the trie node 'eye' exists only as keyword with suggestions (from name parts of e.g. 'eye' — the 👁️ emoji is named 'eye'!). So trie.search('eye') has code (👁️ is named "eye"). Then when text ':eye:' replaced to '👁️ ', cursor...

Alternatively the real difference per the issue: heart and joy suggestions close automatically. Why? Because their trie entries have no 'suggestions' metadata propagation issue... In suggestEmojis:

```
for (const node of nodes) {
    if (node.metaData?.code ...) matching.push(...)
    const suggestions = node.metaData.suggestions;
    if (!suggestions) {
        return;  // returns undefined!
    }
    ...
}
```

Note `return` (undefined) when a node has no suggestions! So suggestEmojis can return undefined. For 'joy' and 'heart' nodes, maybe metaData.suggestions exists (empty array from creation) — in createTrie, metadata = {..., suggestions: []} so code-nodes have suggestions=[]. Keyword nodes via addKeywordsToTrie also have suggestions. Hmm, so when is suggestions undefined? Trie.update preserves suggestions. So never undefined... except nodes whose metadata lacks suggestions — maybe from update calls... 

